  "scope": "Charge receipt section backing on both I/O directions using the existing I/O slot ownership and check submitted write vector and section capacities before reserving a job. Production column capture and read retain the existing per-column limit. The restore queue reserves by count and payload bytes, links waiting and replacement nodes without allocating, and preserves accounting if a new node request is refused. The physical worker result releases its column wrapper and read credit while the same section survives in the bounded world restore queue.",
